hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16100","He said, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Khawlani narrated to me, he said, Umar ibn Rubah al-Taghlibi narrated to me, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa al-Laythi, he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman takes three inheritances, her freed one, and her foundling, and her child for whom she invoked mutual cursing."
"16101","He said: Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Malik al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani informed us, from Bishr ibn Hayyan, he said: Wathilah ibn al-Asqa came to us while we were building our mosque, so he stood over us and greeted us, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever builds a mosque in which prayer is performed, Allah Almighty builds for him in Paradise better than it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it from Haytham ibn Kharijah."
"16102","He said: Attab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, he said: Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Habib, narrated to me that Rabiah ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi informed him, from Wathilah, meaning Ibn al-Asqa, he said: I was of the people of al-Suffah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day called for a loaf, broke it in the bowl, put hot water in it, then put fat in it, then crumbled it, then mixed it, then heaped it, then said: Go and bring me ten, you being the tenth of them. So I brought them to him, and he said: Eat, and eat from its lower part, and do not eat from its upper part, for blessing descends from its upper part. So they ate from it until they were full."
"16103","He said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Malih ibn Usamah, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded with the siwak until I feared it would be prescribed upon me."
"16104","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, he said: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The greatest fabrications are three: that a man fabricate against his eyes, saying: I saw, though he did not see, and that he fabricate against his parents, being claimed to other than his father, or saying: He heard from me, though he did not hear from me."
"16105","He said: Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abu Fadalh al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Abu Sad narrated to us, he said: I saw Wathilah ibn al-Asqa praying in the mosque of Damascus, and he spat under his left foot then rubbed it with his foot. When he finished I said: You are of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), you spit in the mosque? He said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"16106","He said: Abu al-Nadr Hashim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ulathah informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, he said: A group from Banu Sulaym came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a companion of ours has made punishment due. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him free a Muslim slave; Allah Almighty will free, for each limb of it, a limb of him from the Fire."
"16107","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid al-Himsi narrated to us, from Abu Salamah al-Himsi, he said: Umar ibn Rubah al-Taghlibi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Abdullah al-Nasri narrated to us, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman takes possession of three inheritances: her freed slave, her foundling, and her child over whom she invokes lian."
"16108","He said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from al-Gharif al-Daylami, he said: We came to Wathilah ibn al-Asqa al-Laythi and said: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a companion of ours who had made punishment due, and he said: Free a slave on his behalf; Allah Almighty will free, for each limb, a limb of him from the Fire."
"16109","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar, meaning al-Razi, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Malik, he said: Abu Siba narrated to us, he said: I bought a she-camel from the house of Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, and when I went out with it, Wathilah caught up with us while dragging his cloak, and said: O Abdullah, did you buy? I said: Yes. He said: Did he clarify to you what is in her? I said: And what is in her? He said: She is fat, outwardly healthy. He said: Did you intend a journey with her or did you intend meat with her? I said: Rather I intended to perform Hajj on her. He said: In her hoof there is a hole. Then its owner said: May Allah set you right, why do you spoil it for me? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It is not lawful for anyone selling a thing except to clarify what is in it, nor is it lawful for one who knows that except to clarify it."
"16110","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from Abu Malih ibn Usamah, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed one of the hadd punishments of Allah Almighty, so carry out the hadd of Allah in me. So he turned away, then he came to him a second time, and he turned away from him, then he said it a third time, and he turned away from him, then the prayer was established, and when he finished the prayer he came to him a fourth time and said: I have committed one of the hadd punishments of Allah Almighty, so carry out in me the hadd of Allah Almighty. He said: So he called him and said: Did you not perform ablution well, then witness the prayer with us just now? He said: Yes. He said: Go, for it is your expiation."
"16111","He said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Rabiah ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi narrated to me, he said: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The greatest lie is three: that a man lie about his eyes, saying: I saw, though he did not see, and that he lie about his parents, being claimed to other than his father, and that he say: I heard, though he did not hear."
"16112","He said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Sulayman, meaning Ibn Abi al-Saib, narrated to me, he said: Hayyan Abu al-Nadr narrated to me, he said: I entered with Wathilah ibn al-Asqa upon Abu al-Aswad al-Jurashi in his illness in which he died, and he greeted him and sat. Abu al-Aswad took the right hand of Wathilah and wiped with it over his eyes and face, because of his pledge with it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Wathilah said to him: One thing I ask you about. He said: And what is it? He said: How is your opinion of your Lord? Abu al-Aswad said, motioning with his head, meaning: Good. Wathilah said: Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah Almighty said: I am at the opinion of My servant of Me, so let him think of Me what he wills."
"16113","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz and Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated to me that they both heard it from Hayyan Abu al-Nadr narrating it, and they do not attain the memorization of al-Walid ibn Sulayman."
"16114","He said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Janah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed so-and-so son of so-and-so is in Thy protection and the rope of Thy neighboring, so shield him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Fire. Thou art the people of faithfulness and truth. O Allah, forgive him and have mercy on him, for Thou art the Forgiving, the Merciful."
"16115","He said: al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Shaybah Yahya ibn Yazid, from Abd al-Wahhab al-Makki, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abdullah al-Nasri, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is inviolable to the Muslim: his blood, his honor, and his wealth. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him nor forsake him. And piety is here, and he motioned with his hand to the heart. He said: And sufficient evil for a man is to despise his Muslim brother."
